.TH DREAMCATCHER 1 "August 2026" "dreamcatcher 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dreamcatcher \- compile .dream files into .deliver execution contracts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dreamcatcher
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Dreamcatcher is the compiler of the Dream suite. It discovers
\fB.dream\fR files, builds a Dream IR graph, runs deterministic analysis
passes (clustering, conflict detection, dependency resolution, synthesis,
prioritisation) and emits \fB.deliver\fR execution contracts for Dreamboat.
.PP
Dreams are possibilities. Delivers are decisions. Dreamboat is action.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-root \ \fIDIR\fR
Discovery root (repeatable; default: current directory).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config \ \fIPATH\fR
Config file path (default: built\-in defaults).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-out \ \fIDIR\fR
Output directory (default: ./deliverables).
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format \ \fITEXT|JSON\fR
Report format (default: text).
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Analyse and report without writing deliverables.
.TP
.B \-\-strict
Treat warnings as errors.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B validate
Parse\-check all .dream files without emitting.
.TP
.B ir [\-\-emit \fIPATH\fR]
Dump the Dream IR graph as JSON.
.TP
.B init
Write a commented dreamcatcher.toml template.
.TP
.B schema
Print the JSON Schema of the .dream format.
.TP
.B completions \fISHELL\fR
Generate shell completions.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on parse errors / dangling references / dependency cycles,
2 on warnings in \-\-strict mode.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I *.dream
TOML dream input files.
.TP
.I deliverables/<slug>.deliver
YAML execution contracts with provenance.
.TP
.I deliverables/<slug>.deliver.json
Dreamboat\-compatible JSON sidecars.
.TP
.I deliverables/manifest.json
The deliver DAG in priority order.
.SH SEE ALSO
dreamboat(1), deliver(1)
